rlm-gae-version-rm [-n|--dry-run] [-f|--force] [-p PROJECT]...

Multi-select App Engine versions in an fzf picker and delete them.
Versions are listed oldest first across every configured project,
annotated with age, project, service, traffic split and serving
status. Deleting a version is what makes its Artifact Registry image
reclaimable, so this is the first half of a registry cleanup; sweep
the images afterwards with gar-version-rm or a repository cleanup
policy.

Versions receiving traffic are hidden by default. The API refuses to
delete them, but it refuses at the end of the batch, after everything
else is already gone -- filtering them out turns a partial failure
into something that cannot be selected. Pass -f to re-admit them, for
the case where traffic has been migrated and the listing is stale.

Before deleting, the exact gcloud command is printed one argument per
line, one call per (project, service) group. Selecting every version
of a service is called out separately, since that service will not
serve again until it is redeployed. After the delete, each service is
re-listed and the selected ids are checked: a clean exit code is not
treated as proof.

The picker reopens after each successful round so several projects
can be cleaned up in one sitting. Ctrl-G exits.

WHY THIS IS NOT A REGISTRY RECONCILE

App Engine standard does not publish the Artifact Registry image
backing a version: gcloud app versions describe returns
deployment.container as null and fills only deployment.files. There
is therefore no supported way to compute which GAR images no live
version still references, and correlating by timestamp is ambiguous
(one sampled version had ten same-day candidate images). Deleting on
that guess destroys the image behind a serving version and only
surfaces at rollback. Google's documented order is the reverse:
delete the version, then reclaim the artifacts.

ARGUMENTS
  -n, --dry-run  Show the commands that would run; delete nothing.
  -f, --force    Also offer versions currently receiving traffic.
  -p, --project  Limit to this project. Repeatable. Overrides the
                 environment variables below.

ENVIRONMENT
  GAE_SEARCH_PROJECTS  Colon-separated project ids to scan
                       (optional; falls back to the variable below).
  GAR_SEARCH_PROJECTS  Used when GAE_SEARCH_PROJECTS is unset, since
                       App Engine and its registry repository live in
                       the same projects.

REQUIRES
  gcloud, fzf, jq, python3
